<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Ralsko and Vranovské skály loop — Ralsko and Vranovské skály loop [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>Start on the walking street by Mimoň railway station and follow red through the town square and Vranov. Visit the marked Juliina viewpoint and return to red, then climb via Sedlo to the Ralsko summit castle ruins and return to Sedlo. Continue down the northern red forest course, turn left onto the wide track at the T-junction and reach the public road to Srní Potok. Follow blue along the road, turn right onto the shared cyclepath, then return through Mimoň centre to the same station walking street. The optional unmarked western summit ridge is excluded.

Plan this walk for snow-free daylight in spring, summer or autumn. The steep sandstone and basalt paths, steps and summit ground can be rough and slippery, especially when wet or icy. Stay on marked tourist paths in the reserves, respect habitat protection and avoid climbing protected sandstone towers or taking the unmarked western ridge. Check current conservation signs, forestry restrictions, gate passage and construction around the station before walking; closed or prohibited required ground makes this itinerary unavailable. Watch for traffic on road and shared cyclepath sections, and check train services separately.

The complete course is approximately 13.8 km, calculated from the captured OpenStreetMap path. Allow about 270 minutes; the inherited 460 m ascent and 460 m descent figures are approximate estimates, not an elevation survey. Geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0, from the complete captured API XML. This is a descriptive planning route, not navigation-grade, and contains no elevation data.

